Subject: [PATCH] Revert "net: qrtr: Send HELLO message on endpoint register"

Revert upstream 544d85de4dc22c01badfd8cefa59829ce35c4858 for the
Romulus13 kernel build until a complete upstream resume fix is available.

ath12k powers down firmware during system suspend while retaining its
MHI/QRTR endpoint. Resume restarts firmware without registering a new
endpoint, so the new registration-only HELLO is never sent again. The
commit also removed the nameserver reply to incoming HELLO. On WCN7850,
resume receives HELLO but never discovers the WLAN QMI service and times
out waiting for restart completion.

Restore the preceding handshake implementation. Tested on Romulus13 with
Ubuntu 7.3.0-5.5, WCN7850 firmware WLAN.HMT.1.1.c7-00108 and Secure Boot:
deep resume discovers service 0x45 about 3 ms after HELLO and reconnects
Wi-Fi with the original PCIe D3cold policy. Disabling D3cold alone did not
fix the regression. See docs/7.3-wifi-resume.zh-CN.md for test scope.

Apply only if the introduced code is present. The reviewed optional
series also recognizes the complete postimage on unaffected 7.2 sources;
unknown changes fail the build for review. No contributor sign-off is
claimed by this local revert.

Upstream: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/544d85de4dc22c01badfd8cefa59829ce35c4858

